  "confidence": 0.85,
  "summary": "A checkpoint rewrote delete blocks for commits above its visibility bound and, for unchanged row groups, could leave persisted delete blocks unmarked as in use, so a concurrent delete let them be freed and the table later failed to load during WAL replay; the fix tracks the oldest pending delete commit and only writes or marks blocks when that commit is below the bound.",
